# 27. SQLAlchemy Relationships

Two important concepts:

### ForeignKey

```python
owner_id = mapped_column(
    ForeignKey("users.id")
)
```

**Database-level relationship.**

### relationship()

```python
owner = relationship(
    "User",
    back_populates="complaints"
)
```

**Python/ORM-level navigation.**

Example:

```python
complaint.owner
```

and:

```python
user.complaints
```

### Remember:

```text
ForeignKey
→ database connection

relationship()
→ Python/ORM navigation
```

---

# 28. One-to-Many

One user can have many complaints:

```text
User
 ↓
Complaint
Complaint
Complaint
```

Example:

```python
user.complaints
```

returns multiple Complaint objects.

