# 53. Most Important Interview One-Liners

### ORM

> ORM maps application objects to relational database structures.

### Engine

> Engine manages database connectivity and connection pooling.

### Session

> Session is the working unit for ORM operations and transaction management.

### Flush

> Flush sends pending changes to the database without committing the transaction.

### Commit

> Commit commits the current transaction.

### Rollback

> Rollback undoes the current uncommitted transaction and resets the failed transaction state.

### Primary Key

> Uniquely identifies a row.

### Foreign Key

> References a key in another table and maintains referential integrity.

### Index

> Data structure that improves lookup performance at storage and write-maintenance cost.

### Transaction

> Groups multiple operations into one atomic unit.

### MVCC

> PostgreSQL's multi-version concurrency mechanism that enables concurrent transactions with consistent reads and reduced blocking.

### Alembic

> Database migration tool used to version and apply SQLAlchemy schema changes.

### Repository

> Handles database access.

### Service

> Handles business logic.

### Router

> Handles HTTP communication.

